-- title:
--   Diamond action on the mod-ℓ q-expansion function field of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $\ell \nmid M$, and $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$; write $\Gamma_H(M) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry, as a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$, lies in $H$, and let $F$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Z}/\ell \subseteq (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)((q))$ generated by all quotients $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), $p_f,p_g$ are integral power series whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at $\infty$, and the reduction $\bar p_g$ of $p_g$ modulo $\ell$, read as a Laurent series, is nonzero. The assertion is that there is a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(M)$ to the group of $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$-algebra automorphisms of $F$ such that: (i) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$, every weight $k$, every form $f$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ of weight $k$ and every integral $q$-expansion $p$ of $f$, there are $n \in \mathbb{N}$, a form $f_1$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ of weight $k$ with $f_1 = M^n\,(f\mid_k \gamma)$ as functions on the upper half plane, and an integral $q$-expansion $p_1$ of $f_1$, with $\bar p_1 = 0$ if and only if $\bar p = 0$; (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$, weight $k$, forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$, satisfying $f_1 = f\mid_k\gamma$ and $g_1 = g\mid_k\gamma$ pointwise and $\bar p_g \neq 0$, every $x \in F$ whose underlying Laurent series is $\bar p_{f_1}/\bar p_{g_1}$ has $\rho(\gamma)(x)$ equal, as a Laurent series, to $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$; (iii) $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ whenever $\gamma$ lies in [`CohCarrier.GammaH M (H ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1))`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133); (iv) the field [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFullC (ZMod ℓ) M`](def/ModularCurve_X0ModL.html#L100), generated over $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$ by the series $q \mapsto$ $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M$, is contained in $F$; and (v) each $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes every element of $F$ whose Laurent series lies in that subfield.
--
--   This is the mod-$\ell$ incarnation, on $q$-expansions at $\infty$, of the action of the diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$, $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, on the function field of the modular curve $X_H(M)$, the integrality of the slash action up to powers of $M$ playing the role of the $q$-expansion principle over $\mathbb{Z}[1/M]$. It is used downstream to bound fibres of the $j$-map on $F$ over the full modular function field, to transport the automorphisms along algebra extensions in characteristic $\ell$, and in the construction of Hecke and diamond lifts.
